# Vision Access — environment. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
# .env* is gitignored; no key here ever reaches the browser.

# --- Transit data (build-time only) -----------------------------------
# Auth is the `x-api-key` HEADER. Also accepted: `apikey` header, `?apikey=`.
# Authorization: Bearer does NOT work.
# The gateway rate-limits with a bare 401 {"message":"Unauthorized"} — not a
# 429 — and the lockout is account-wide, not endpoint-scoped, for ~14 minutes.
HAMUGA_API_KEY=

# --- TTS (build-time only) --------------------------------------------
# Provider selection. One of: azure | chimege | mms
TTS_PROVIDER=azure
TTS_VOICE=mn-MN-YesuiNeural

# Azure Speech. F0 free tier = 500,000 characters/month, HARD CAPPED.
# The build prints cumulative usage and aborts rather than exceeding it.
#
# NOW ALSO USED AT RUNTIME, server-side only, by app/api/stt/route.ts — the
# speech-to-text fallback for spoken destinations. Same key, same region, same
# account; it never reaches the browser. Two consequences worth knowing:
#   - STT and TTS bill against DIFFERENT free-tier allowances, but a paid tier
#     is one subscription, so a runaway client affects both.
#   - Azure's STT language list is SEPARATE from its TTS voice list. Having
#     mn-MN-YesuiNeural does NOT prove an mn-MN recognizer exists. Verify
#     before shipping; app/api/stt/route.ts is the only file that changes if a
#     different STT provider is needed.
AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=southeastasia

# Chimege. Kept as an alternate provider. Free tier stops at 100 requests;
# accepts Cyrillic plus ? ! . - ' " : , and 400s on digits, slashes and Latin.
CHIMEGE_TOKEN=

# MMS (facebook/mms-tts-mon) — local Python fallback, no account, no network.
# CC-BY-NC 4.0: NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY. Mongolian dialect quality unverified.
# MMS_PYTHON=.venv-tts/bin/python
# MMS_MODEL=facebook/mms-tts-mon

# --- Pilot scope ------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated route ids. Renders only stops on those routes, plus all
# numbers and fixed phrases. Unset renders the whole city.
# TTS_ROUTES=11100730,11100350,11100612,11101800

# --- Optional model layer (LLM) ---------------------------------------
# ENTIRELY OPTIONAL. Unset = the app runs exactly as it did before: the
# deterministic matcher in lib/routing/resolveJourney.ts answers every
# destination, at ~95% on a clean-room sample. Nothing below can make that
# path worse; it can only add to it.
#
# Two consumers, and they are very different risks:
#
#   BUILD TIME  scripts/generate-stop-aliases.ts proposes the names riders
#               actually say ("Их дэлгүүр" for "Улсын их дэлгүүр"). Runs once,
#               offline, output is human-reviewed before it ships. This is the
#               high-value, no-risk use.
#   RUNTIME     app/api/stop-resolve/route.ts reranks candidates the matcher
#               already found, and only when it is unsure. It can never name a
#               stop that is not already a candidate — see the gate in
#               lib/llm/stop-resolve.ts and its tests.
#
# One of: gemini | groq | openrouter. Leave unset to run without a model.
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini

# Gemini — the default recommendation: best Mongolian of the free tiers.
# Free key, no card: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Free tier ~10 req/min and ~500/day on 2.5-flash; flash-lite is 15/min, 1000/day.
#
# ⚠️ PRIVACY: Google's terms permit training on FREE-TIER prompts. The runtime
# route sends the transcript and candidate stop NAMES only — no coordinates, no
# device id, no history (enforced in sanitizeRequest, not by convention). Even
# so, a rider's spoken destination now leaves the phone, which is a change to
# this app's posture and is worth telling riders about.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite
# GEMINI_API_ENDPOINT=            # set to "legacy" for :generateContent

# Groq — fastest by far, most generous free tier (30/min, ~14,400/day), but its
# free lineup handles Cyrillic Mongolian less reliably. https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-32b

# OpenRouter — one key, many models; good for A/B-ing. Free tier is only ~50
# requests/day until $10 of credit, which is too tight for the alias build.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free
